     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. The reason you gave, timing around the family visit and evening rounds, doesn't address the safety problem. 6,400 mg/day is double the maximum labeled dose. The extra dose adds risk of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, and it is unlikely to add analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit, because ibuprofen's effect plateaus at lower doses.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n\nIf the aim is stronger pain control or anti-inflammatory coverage, I can also enter a multimodal regimen, such as scheduled acetaminophen with ibuprofen at a standard dose. If you have a specific clinical reason for going beyond the maximum, a clinical pharmacist consult is the right route. Pharmacy can then verify and document the order under your hospital's policy.\n\nTell me which option you'd like, and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
